Z||000005||Earl||12-31-2001||04:50 PM||||  Sorry but they discontinued the header and since it was a order on demand Item no one I have called has any in stock.<BR>   I have done some research and learned a few things that I will share .<BR> <BR>1. The 2.5 in the S10 has a stronger block and crank.<P>2. The 87 and later tech 4 has roller lifters. <P>3. The intake and exhaust is where you will see the best bang for your buck.<P>4. This is the best place for information on anything "FIERO"||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJones||12-31-2001||05:06 PM||||I had my old 87 Tech 4 rebuilt by a friend who builds race engines for use out here at RMR.  He ported it, crane cam, etc etc etc..  Total for the entire re-build, PLUS R&R was $900.  I dont know what all was done, but when the car was done, It would keep up with a GT.   No lie, no NOS, no powerchip, stock intake, and a New free flow Exhaust. (the exhaust was not part of the $900, it was $200 at a muffler shop).  It was pushing over 115 horse, off our rough calculations, and still got upper 20's, low 30's mpg.  It's possible, just hard to do.  My rebuld took 3 weeks, all from waiting on parts.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrossum||12-31-2001||09:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Earl:<BR><B>  Sorry but they discontinued the header and since it was a order on demand Item no one I have called has any in stock.<BR>   I have done some research and learned a few things that I will share .<BR> <BR>1. The 2.5 in the S10 has a stronger block and crank.<P>2. The 87 and later tech 4 has roller lifters. <P>3. The intake and exhaust is where you will see the best bang for your buck.<P>4. This is the best place for information on anything "FIERO"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>s10 block won't work. starter is on wrong side. <BR>crank is same as any other non-dis 2.5 gm engine.<BR>i used an early nova 153 crank in my stroker motor. gained .250" in stroke. Crower big block chev stainless roller rockers, screw in studs and locks. 1.8 intake ratio, 1.7 exhaust. Crower 6 inch sportsman rods. Schneider custom grind roller cam. home made adapter to use small block chev 2bbl throttle body on stock (massively ported on intake port) intake. once i get the wiring and brain figured out, will have dyno numbers for everyone............<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||12-31-2001||09:17 PM||||Don't forget about Mercury Marine engine parts. I used to have an old Riverside boat powered by a 150 horsepower 181 c.i. duke. We would run it at 4500+ rpms out in the channels for several minutes at a time and it never gave any problems.||||reg||1
